WEBVTT

00:00.700 --> 00:03.204
Neuron is a live engine.

00:03.254 --> 00:05.964
Every point is a word it knows.

00:06.014 --> 00:09.569
Every line is a connection it has made for itself.

00:10.384 --> 00:13.860
Ask it to define a word it has never been given.

00:15.184 --> 00:21.255
It reads its sources, and works the word into the graph, along with every word it met on the way.

00:21.305 --> 00:23.430
Twenty-nine runs.

00:23.480 --> 00:25.761
Thirteen new words.

00:25.811 --> 00:27.699
Two seconds.

00:28.309 --> 00:36.967
One typed line, and a tree of runs underneath it: the engine asking its own questions, and answering them, without being told to.

00:37.518 --> 00:40.998
Ask the same thing again, and nothing runs.

00:41.048 --> 00:43.173
It already knows.

00:43.223 --> 00:46.832
Learning happens once, and takes its time.

00:46.882 --> 00:49.121
Recall is immediate.

00:49.727 --> 00:52.187
A meaning is not fixed.

00:54.936 --> 00:59.389
It can be told, and it can be changed, in a single line.

00:59.936 --> 01:04.232
Every run leaves a receipt: the path it took through the graph.

01:06.936 --> 01:12.144
Any run can be played back, hop by hop, and every hop can be read.

01:16.336 --> 01:17.889
Neuron.

01:17.939 --> 01:21.470
Research and engineering by James Huson.

01:21.520 --> 01:23.681
exnulla dot com.
